          "final_text_tail": "   @internalcode\n    def load(\n        self,\n        environment: \"Environment\",\n        name: str,\n        globals: t.Optional[t.MutableMapping[str, t.Any]] = None,\n    ) -> \"Template\":\n        name = self._resolve_alias(name)\n        name = self._transform_path(name)\n        key = self.get_template_key(name)\n        module = f\"{self.package_name}.{key}\"\n        mod = getattr(self.module, module, None)\n\n        if mod is None:\n            try:\n                mod = __import__(module, None, None, [\"root\"])\n            except ImportError as e:\n                raise TemplateNotFound(name) from e\n\n            # remove the entry from sys.modules, we only want the attribute\n            # on the module object we have stored on the loader.\n            sys.modules.pop(module, None)\n\n        if globals is None:\n            globals = {}\n\n        return environment.template_class.from_module_dict(\n            environment, mod.__dict__, globals\n        )\n```\n\nVerification to run once the file is written (I could not execute these in this read-only session): `python -m pytest tests/ -v`, `mypy`, and `black --check src/jinja2/loaders.py` + `flake8 src/jinja2/loaders.py`. Behavior notes: all new parameters/keywords are optional so existing calls are untouched; `TemplateNotFound` carries the alias-resolved (target) name when an alias was used and the original untransformed name otherwise; alias lookup is a single dict get so aliases never chain; `remove_alias` is a no-op for unknown aliases.",
