          "final_text_tail": "pass and my 26-point feature verification (run and then cleaned up) passed completely.\n\n**Changes** \u2014 all in `src/jinja2/loaders.py`:\n\n**Task 1 \u2014 `path_transform`** (src/jinja2/loaders.py:74):\n- New optional `path_transform: t.Optional[t.Callable[[str], str]] = None` kwarg on `BaseLoader.__init__` and every loader: `FileSystemLoader`, `PackageLoader`, `DictLoader`, `FunctionLoader`, `PrefixLoader`, `ChoiceLoader` (plus `ModuleLoader` for consistency).\n- A shared `BaseLoader._prepare_template()` helper (src/jinja2/loaders.py:95) resolves aliases, then applies the transform, returning `(reported_name, resolved_name)`.\n- Applied at the top of every `get_source`, and in the `load` overrides of `PrefixLoader`/`ChoiceLoader` (top level, before delegating to children).\n- `TemplateNotFound` reports the original pre-transform name; transform exceptions propagate; `None`/omitted = unchanged behavior.\n\n**Task 2 \u2014 aliases** (src/jinja2/loaders.py:80):\n- `BaseLoader.add_alias(alias, target)` and `remove_alias(alias)` (safe no-op for missing aliases, overwritable).\n- Single-hop resolution in `_prepare_template` \u2014 no recursive chaining \u2014 applied before normal lookup in all loaders.\n- Broken aliases raise `TemplateNotFound` referencing the target name (verified via `e.name` and `str(e)`); alias names can be any string including `\"\"`.\n\nAssumption noted: when both features apply, alias resolution runs first, then the transform \u2014 this satisfies both specs' error-name requirements independently.",
